+## Keys and roles
+
+Send `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are in the data as
+`apiKeys: [{ key, name, role }]`. `viewer` may only GET; `cook` may also
+`POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`, `POST /temperatures` and
+`POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`; `manager` may do everything. Without a key or
+with an unknown key the answer is 401 `unauthorized`; without permission it is
+403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request by a known key that is not a GET is written to `audit`
+(`at`, `key` name, `method`, `path`, `status`). `GET /audit` lists the entries
+newest first and is for managers only.
